opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Choice-tape shrinking for base_quickcheck, ported from Hypothesis"
description: """
A port of Hypothesis's Conjecture choice-tape engine to base_quickcheck.
Shrinking works on the recorded sequence of PRNG draws rather than on a
rose tree, so it shrinks unmodified base_quickcheck generators.

base_quickcheck, ppx_quickcheck and splittable_random are vendored (the
last carries a small addition, For_tape.attach, needed to record draws),
so they are not listed as dependencies here.

NOT YET INSTALLABLE AS AN OPAM PACKAGE. The libraries have no
public_name, and cannot until the vendored splittable_random fork is
resolved: a public library may not depend on a private one, and
For_tape.attach is not upstream. That is what
https://github.com/janestreet/splittable_random/pull/2 blocks.

Until then this file exists so that `opam install . --deps-only` works
in CI and for contributors. The build command below deliberately builds
the whole tree rather than `-p tape`, because `-p tape` currently
selects nothing at all and would succeed vacuously.
"""
maintainer: "Matthias Goergens <matthias.goergens@gmail.com>"
authors: "Matthias Goergens"
license: "MIT"
homepage: "https://github.com/matthiasgoergens/tapecheck"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/matthiasgoergens/tapecheck/issues"
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/matthiasgoergens/tapecheck.git"
depends: [
  "ocaml" {>= "5.1.0"}
  "dune" {>= "3.9"}
  "base"
  "stdio"
  "ppxlib"
  "ppxlib_jane"
  "ppx_base"
  "ppx_compare"
  "ppx_fields_conv"
  "ppx_let"
  "ppx_sexp_conv"
  "ppx_sexp_message"
  "ppx_sexp_value"
]
depopts: [
  "qcheck"
]
build: [
  ["dune" "build" "-j" jobs]
]
